12
00:00:54,604 --> 00:00:55,813
Ms. Da-reum.

13
00:00:56,355 --> 00:00:58,232
I'm not into men.

14
00:00:58,983 --> 00:01:00,234
- What?
- Also...

15
00:01:02,069 --> 00:01:03,863
there's this woman
I'm interested in right now.

16
00:01:05,656 --> 00:01:06,699
What?

17
00:01:38,272 --> 00:01:39,315
Director Lee.

18
00:01:39,857 --> 00:01:40,942
How did you find us here?

19
00:01:51,744 --> 00:01:52,912
I heard about the covert op.

20
00:01:53,829 --> 00:01:56,707
Ms. Kim told me that you had trouble
trying to get Master Im on board.

21
00:01:57,291 --> 00:01:58,376
I came out to help.

22
00:01:59,168 --> 00:02:00,169
At this hour?

23
00:02:00,711 --> 00:02:01,754
Did you really come for work?

24
00:02:01,837 --> 00:02:04,632
Of course.
I'm that serious about work.

25
00:02:11,138 --> 00:02:12,181
{\an8}So, well...

26
00:02:12,807 --> 00:02:14,809
{\an8}There are only two rooms.

27
00:02:15,017 --> 00:02:16,435
{\an8}I can crash in his room.

28
00:02:17,436 --> 00:02:19,730
{\an8}- You, in my room?
- It's not like I can take her room.

29
00:02:21,983 --> 00:02:23,985
{\an8}Well, that wasn't what I meant.

30
00:02:24,235 --> 00:02:26,195
{\an8}It's nothing new between us.

31
00:02:30,616 --> 00:02:31,701
{\an8}Get away from me.

32
00:02:35,413 --> 00:02:37,957
{\an8}I won't misunderstand
the situation anymore, Mr. Kang.

33
00:02:38,040 --> 00:02:39,041
{\an8}Don't worry.

34
00:02:39,584 --> 00:02:40,585
{\an8}"Misunderstand"?

35
00:02:41,002 --> 00:02:43,296
{\an8}Well, if it's
too inconvenient for you

36
00:02:43,379 --> 00:02:45,673
{\an8}I can sleep out in the hall.

37
00:02:46,007 --> 00:02:48,342
{\an8}No, you should take one of the rooms.

38
00:02:48,718 --> 00:02:50,469
- I'll share mine with him.
- Okay.

39
00:02:51,178 --> 00:02:52,555
Okay. Then it's decided.

40
00:02:52,805 --> 00:02:53,848
We'll take this one.

41
00:02:55,433 --> 00:02:58,436
- Good night.
- Have a good rest.

42
00:03:13,284 --> 00:03:15,453
<i>You have a thing
for Director Lee Chan.</i>

43
00:03:15,536 --> 00:03:18,247
For a long time.

44
00:03:20,791 --> 00:03:21,834
I mean, me?

45
00:03:23,502 --> 00:03:25,671
- Jeez.
- Da-reum is unbelievable.

46
00:03:25,755 --> 00:03:28,382
What about me gives off that vibe?

47
00:03:34,930 --> 00:03:36,474
Are you disappointed

48
00:03:36,724 --> 00:03:37,975
that she doesn't think of you
as a man?

49
00:03:38,059 --> 00:03:39,060
Whatever.

50
00:03:39,935 --> 00:03:40,936
Gosh.

51
00:03:46,817 --> 00:03:47,818
I can tell

52
00:03:49,362 --> 00:03:50,946
that you care about Da-reum.

53
00:03:52,406 --> 00:03:53,741
Concerned? Hardly.

54
00:03:55,618 --> 00:03:57,161
She's new to work.

55
00:03:57,244 --> 00:03:58,537
That's why I'm looking out for her.

56
00:04:02,958 --> 00:04:05,586
Looking out for someone and actually
caring for them aren't the same.

57
00:04:07,338 --> 00:04:08,422
It's different.

58
00:04:20,309 --> 00:04:21,644
Wait, Ms. Nam.

59
00:04:23,896 --> 00:04:25,523
- What?
- Also...

60
00:04:26,399 --> 00:04:28,109
there's this woman
I'm interested in right now.

61
00:04:30,444 --> 00:04:31,445
What?

62
00:04:46,252 --> 00:04:48,295
<i>I could see today
that you two have grown close.</i>

63
00:04:49,338 --> 00:04:52,049
I had a feeling
that you might be interested in her.

64
00:04:54,844 --> 00:04:55,845
I'm not.

65
00:04:57,096 --> 00:04:58,139
Even if I did

66
00:04:59,098 --> 00:05:00,933
it's impossible for a CEO
to date a rookie.

67
00:05:22,830 --> 00:05:25,583
So Mr. Kang wasn't into men.

68
00:05:27,334 --> 00:05:30,421
Who's the woman he's interested in?

69
00:05:39,722 --> 00:05:40,890
Come on, Da-reum.

70
00:05:41,432 --> 00:05:44,518
Why do you want to know that?

71
00:05:44,935 --> 00:05:46,061
Come on.

72
00:05:48,439 --> 00:05:51,108
Could it be someone at work?

73
00:06:35,236 --> 00:06:36,987
Yes, just like that.

74
00:06:37,071 --> 00:06:38,113
Don't let it get tangled.

75
00:06:38,197 --> 00:06:39,949
Like that.

76
00:06:40,032 --> 00:06:42,117
That's it. Carefully.

77
00:06:42,201 --> 00:06:43,577
Okay. Good.

78
00:06:46,622 --> 00:06:47,706
You have a knack for this.

79
00:06:52,878 --> 00:06:54,421
Did you have trouble sleeping too?

80
00:06:56,006 --> 00:06:57,049
Yes.

81
00:06:57,758 --> 00:06:59,301
And I saw the light was on.

82
00:07:00,886 --> 00:07:02,179
Come here and join me.

83
00:07:04,807 --> 00:07:05,808
May I?

84
00:07:09,144 --> 00:07:11,981
It's best to move your hands
when you're stressed out.

85
00:07:12,606 --> 00:07:14,483
Knotting may seem like a job
where you tie things

86
00:07:14,567 --> 00:07:17,444
but you'll come to learn
that it can untangle your heart.

87
00:07:18,612 --> 00:07:21,615
You're right.
Tying knots helped me clear my head.

88
00:07:23,784 --> 00:07:25,911
- You should give it a go too.
- Okay.

89
00:07:26,161 --> 00:07:27,955
- Do what you did yesterday.
- Okay.

90
00:07:35,754 --> 00:07:38,465
I let my feelings
get ahead of me yesterday.

91
00:07:38,966 --> 00:07:40,551
I shouldn't have said it like that.

92
00:07:42,928 --> 00:07:45,639
So even if Master Im
doesn't agree to be on board

93
00:07:46,098 --> 00:07:49,143
I hope you two can make
these traditional knots more visible.

94
00:07:51,520 --> 00:07:54,189
We completely understand
what you mean.

95
00:07:55,858 --> 00:07:58,903
I'm happy to know that you do.

96
00:08:00,404 --> 00:08:02,698
Please continue to practice.
I'll get breakfast ready.

97
00:08:03,073 --> 00:08:04,742
- Sure.
- And this one.

98
00:08:05,117 --> 00:08:06,577
I'm taking your first knot.

99
00:08:12,791 --> 00:08:15,294
Ta-da. I made a new one.

100
00:08:15,544 --> 00:08:16,879
I learned it just now.

101
00:08:16,962 --> 00:08:19,131
- You've learned it already?
- Yes.

102
00:08:20,090 --> 00:08:22,134
Do you want me to teach you?

103
00:08:22,760 --> 00:08:23,802
Sure.

104
00:08:24,219 --> 00:08:25,262
Let's do it.

105
00:08:26,138 --> 00:08:28,223
All right. Take a good look.

106
00:08:28,766 --> 00:08:31,518
Put the green cord
on top of the pink one

107
00:08:31,936 --> 00:08:33,896
and create a knot.

108
00:08:34,521 --> 00:08:37,733
Good. Now do you see this space here?

109
00:08:37,816 --> 00:08:39,610
Spread it out a little.

110
00:08:39,693 --> 00:08:41,612
Look, it's a heart.

111
00:08:43,906 --> 00:08:49,161
Then hold the top
and make a wing on each side.

112
00:08:49,870 --> 00:08:51,956
- A wing...
- Yes.

113
00:08:53,248 --> 00:08:56,543
Then hold the top
and pull it to the side.

114
00:09:20,234 --> 00:09:23,320
The young lady
who came from Seoul made this.

115
00:09:24,697 --> 00:09:26,115
She tried rather hard

116
00:09:26,824 --> 00:09:27,908
after just one day.

117
00:09:34,999 --> 00:09:36,458
Isn't that admirable?

118
00:09:41,922 --> 00:09:42,923
Master Im.

119
00:09:44,133 --> 00:09:46,427
I apologize for yesterday.

120
00:09:47,803 --> 00:09:50,055
I knew your intentions very well.

121
00:09:54,184 --> 00:09:55,769
It's always tough

122
00:09:57,229 --> 00:09:58,522
to be a teacher.

123
00:09:59,106 --> 00:10:01,817
I must always keep an eye
on people's feelings as I proceed...

124
00:10:04,778 --> 00:10:06,238
but at times,
I find myself blurting out words

125
00:10:07,448 --> 00:10:08,907
that can turn into sharp blades.

126
00:10:12,161 --> 00:10:13,245
Are you

127
00:10:13,871 --> 00:10:15,456
apologizing right now?

128
00:10:25,049 --> 00:10:27,342
I was just afraid.

129
00:10:28,177 --> 00:10:32,347
That everything we have stood for
would disappear down that road.

130
00:10:40,439 --> 00:10:42,566
It won't disappear, Master Im.

131
00:11:13,347 --> 00:11:14,598
How beautiful.

132
00:11:16,934 --> 00:11:18,143
These are so pretty.

133
00:11:21,063 --> 00:11:22,564
When did you come out?

134
00:11:24,108 --> 00:11:25,109
Just now.

135
00:11:25,776 --> 00:11:28,320
They looked so pretty from the window

136
00:11:28,862 --> 00:11:30,280
so I came out to see them up close.

137
00:11:46,630 --> 00:11:49,091
I'm sorry for that day.

138
00:11:51,218 --> 00:11:54,888
It had been weighing on my mind
after you left like that.

139
00:11:59,184 --> 00:12:00,269
Please don't mind me.

140
00:12:01,019 --> 00:12:03,605
You suffered from a misunderstanding
because of me.

141
00:12:04,064 --> 00:12:05,274
It must've put you in a tough spot.

142
00:12:06,859 --> 00:12:08,527
She and I had already broken up.

143
00:12:09,903 --> 00:12:11,238
She must've said

144
00:12:11,905 --> 00:12:14,199
all those mean things to you
out of spite for me.

145
00:12:15,701 --> 00:12:16,827
I apologize.

146
00:12:20,038 --> 00:12:21,832
I'm really fine.

147
00:12:28,130 --> 00:12:30,048
I'm okay, really.

148
00:12:37,139 --> 00:12:38,182
Da-reum.

149
00:12:38,515 --> 00:12:40,434
There's something I want to show you.

150
00:12:41,852 --> 00:12:45,147
Can you spare me some time
on our way back to Seoul?

151
00:12:55,532 --> 00:12:57,075
A lot went through my mind

152
00:12:57,993 --> 00:12:59,453
after learning how to make knots.

153
00:13:00,370 --> 00:13:02,623
Traditional knots
are a form of art and meditation

154
00:13:02,831 --> 00:13:04,791
not something
you can print with a machine.

155
00:13:05,500 --> 00:13:07,628
I brought up words
like factory production

156
00:13:07,711 --> 00:13:09,504
without realizing
how deep the practice was.

157
00:13:12,299 --> 00:13:13,300
I apologize.

158
00:13:14,051 --> 00:13:15,344
I apologize.

159
00:13:16,637 --> 00:13:18,472
And because we desperately
wanted to work with you

160
00:13:18,972 --> 00:13:20,849
I also had forgotten
about the core of my business.

161
00:13:21,475 --> 00:13:23,560
Appello strives
to maintain value that will last

162
00:13:24,686 --> 00:13:26,480
instead of fast-paced trends.

163
00:13:28,148 --> 00:13:30,275
So what if we provided
an experience for the people

164
00:13:30,692 --> 00:13:33,654
in the exact traditional way
of your practice?

165
00:13:42,871 --> 00:13:46,208
How about putting together a DIY kit

166
00:13:46,291 --> 00:13:48,085
so people can try making
traditional Korean knots

167
00:13:48,168 --> 00:13:51,588
with all the materials
and instructions at home?

168
00:13:52,589 --> 00:13:55,092
I thought
it was very difficult to make knots

169
00:13:55,175 --> 00:13:57,427
but I had so much fun
when I got my hands on it.

170
00:13:57,761 --> 00:14:00,055
I'm sure many people will love it.

171
00:14:10,274 --> 00:14:11,984
Perhaps it's more meaningful

172
00:14:13,151 --> 00:14:15,946
to have knots
created by many new hands

173
00:14:18,448 --> 00:14:21,368
instead of ones made
by a single artisan.

174
00:14:23,161 --> 00:14:26,248
If you're going to make it,
make it right.

175
00:14:26,748 --> 00:14:28,208
The traditional knot kit.

176
00:14:31,003 --> 00:14:32,129
Thank you, Master Im.

177
00:14:32,212 --> 00:14:34,464
- Thank you, ma'am.
- However...

178
00:14:35,424 --> 00:14:36,633
there is one condition.

179
00:14:37,342 --> 00:14:40,929
I won't allow you to make something
with half-hearted instructions.

180
00:14:41,179 --> 00:14:42,889
They must have hands-on experience

181
00:14:44,099 --> 00:14:46,059
as they learn to make actual knots.

182
00:14:47,394 --> 00:14:50,272
Do you mean that people must
take part in the experience?

183
00:14:50,981 --> 00:14:52,566
That's what will actually last.

184
00:14:53,275 --> 00:14:54,818
I'll see what you come up with

185
00:14:54,901 --> 00:14:57,404
before I go ahead
and give you my final approval.

186
00:15:14,171 --> 00:15:16,548
- Hop in, Ms. Nam.
- Okay.

187
00:15:17,132 --> 00:15:18,967
Ms. Da-reum, let's go in my car.

188
00:15:20,093 --> 00:15:21,428
You'd probably prefer to go alone.

189
00:15:22,471 --> 00:15:24,848
Come with me. His car
isn't built for long-distance trips.

190
00:15:25,682 --> 00:15:28,727
What do you mean?
I'd get there an hour before you.

191
00:15:30,312 --> 00:15:31,355
Hey.

192
00:15:32,064 --> 00:15:33,940
My seats come with a massager.

193
00:15:35,567 --> 00:15:37,444
You can lie down flat on my seat.

194
00:15:43,992 --> 00:15:45,327
Ms. Da-reum,
whose car do you want to take?

195
00:15:48,705 --> 00:15:50,999
First of all,
can you let my hands go?

196
00:15:57,798 --> 00:15:58,840
Then...

197
00:16:01,176 --> 00:16:02,928
<i>I'm sorry for that day.</i>

198
00:16:03,637 --> 00:16:05,764
There's something I want to show you.

199
00:16:05,889 --> 00:16:07,307
Can you spare me some time

200
00:16:07,849 --> 00:16:09,351
on our way back to Seoul?

201
00:16:13,230 --> 00:16:14,481
May I take

202
00:16:15,023 --> 00:16:16,900
Director Lee's car?

203
00:16:16,983 --> 00:16:18,610
You'll also find
that more convenient.

204
00:16:21,154 --> 00:16:22,239
All right, then.

205
00:16:25,492 --> 00:16:26,910
Was my car uncomfortable?

206
00:16:28,537 --> 00:16:31,748
No, it was such a comfortable ride.

207
00:16:31,832 --> 00:16:35,127
I just felt bad
that you always had to give me rides.

208
00:16:38,505 --> 00:16:40,757
I'll take Ms. Da-reum home.

209
00:16:44,386 --> 00:16:45,720
Have a safe trip back.

210
00:16:47,806 --> 00:16:49,015
Thank you.

211
00:16:54,688 --> 00:16:55,772
Hey, Ha-gi.

212
00:16:56,815 --> 00:16:57,899
Drive safely.

213
00:16:58,483 --> 00:16:59,568
Sure.

214
00:17:12,330 --> 00:17:13,665
Do you know where you are?

215
00:17:16,710 --> 00:17:19,796
It's a bus stop in my neighborhood.

216
00:17:27,220 --> 00:17:29,014
{\an8}D.N.X FOREVER
LET'S STAY TOGETHER FOREVER

217
00:17:29,264 --> 00:17:30,515
Oh, this...

218
00:17:31,766 --> 00:17:32,934
You wrote this.

219
00:17:34,186 --> 00:17:35,645
How did you know that?

220
00:17:39,608 --> 00:17:40,859
Do you remember this photo book?

221
00:17:43,737 --> 00:17:45,280
This is...

222
00:17:58,376 --> 00:17:59,461
Chan.

223
00:18:04,007 --> 00:18:05,800
EXCLUSIVE:
WHERE IS D.N.X'S LEE CHAN NOW?

224
