WON-BIN

786
00:57:57,917 --> 00:58:00,711
Maybe something urgent came up.

787
00:58:01,504 --> 00:58:02,713
No, it's fine.

788
00:58:08,135 --> 00:58:09,804
COCOTALK

789
00:58:09,887 --> 00:58:11,806
<i>Chan, it's urgent. Answer your phone.</i>

790
00:58:13,390 --> 00:58:14,850
- Chan.
<i>- Yes.</i>

791
00:58:14,934 --> 00:58:16,560
Why weren't you answering your phone?

792
00:58:16,644 --> 00:58:18,270
I'm outside right now.

793
00:58:18,896 --> 00:58:19,980
What's up?

794
00:58:20,689 --> 00:58:23,859
<i>Director Park Chan-dong
gave us a call.</i>

795
00:58:24,276 --> 00:58:26,320
<i>He wants to see you
at his studio right now.</i>

796
00:58:26,403 --> 00:58:27,905
<i>I guess he liked you at the audition.</i>

797
00:58:28,072 --> 00:58:29,156
Really?

798
00:58:33,953 --> 00:58:35,329
But not now.

799
00:58:37,414 --> 00:58:38,666
This is more important.

800
00:58:38,749 --> 00:58:40,125
<i>Hey. Are you nuts?</i>

801
00:58:40,209 --> 00:58:41,585
<i>This is
a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity.</i>

802
00:58:41,836 --> 00:58:44,505
<i>This could get you to Cannes.</i>

803
00:58:44,964 --> 00:58:47,091
No more nonsense. Wrap it up now.

804
00:58:47,466 --> 00:58:48,926
I'll go pick you up now.

805
00:59:05,109 --> 00:59:06,819
Da-reum, I'm sorry...

806
00:59:09,655 --> 00:59:11,031
Do you have to go?

807
00:59:11,115 --> 00:59:13,325
A meeting just got scheduled
for my next project.

808
00:59:14,326 --> 00:59:16,328
That's really important.

809
00:59:16,412 --> 00:59:19,081
The director's only available
right now.

810
00:59:19,164 --> 00:59:20,165
I'm sorry.

811
00:59:20,374 --> 00:59:22,751
Oh, no. It's okay.

812
00:59:23,168 --> 00:59:24,503
Like you said earlier

813
00:59:24,753 --> 00:59:27,131
you have to prove yourself
as much as you're loved.

814
00:59:27,631 --> 00:59:28,883
Sorry about this, Da-reum.

815
00:59:30,175 --> 00:59:32,803
It's really okay.
You should get going.

816
00:59:33,345 --> 00:59:35,264
- I'll call you.
- Yes.

817
00:59:39,560 --> 00:59:40,561
Go on.

818
00:59:53,240 --> 00:59:54,283
{\an8}Well, then.

819
00:59:54,450 --> 00:59:58,495
{\an8}We'll proceed with the contract
under the terms you proposed, Mr. Kang.

820
00:59:58,746 --> 01:00:01,457
{\an8}Thank you.
I appreciate your flexibility.

821
01:00:06,086 --> 01:00:07,087
{\an8}Thank you.

822
01:00:07,338 --> 01:00:08,676
{\an8}How was the meeting today?

823
01:00:08,756 --> 01:00:10,052
{\an8}I'd say it went very well.

824
01:00:10,132 --> 01:00:11,884
{\an8}- Good news?
- I think so.

825
01:00:29,401 --> 01:00:32,196
Your party
had arranged this in advance.

826
01:00:47,378 --> 01:00:49,213
{\an8}MS. NAM DA-REUM
HAPPY BIRTHDAY

827
01:00:52,007 --> 01:00:53,175
What's she doing alone?

828
01:00:53,884 --> 01:00:56,136
She's looking this way.

829
01:00:56,303 --> 01:00:59,139
That's sad.

830
01:01:00,724 --> 01:01:02,643
HAPPY BIRTHDAY TO NAM DA-REUM

831
01:01:13,445 --> 01:01:15,739
{\an8}<i>Wait, no one showed up for real?</i>

832
01:01:15,823 --> 01:01:17,241
{\an8}LEE YE-JI

833
01:01:17,783 --> 01:01:18,784
<i>Sorry.</i>

834
01:01:19,034 --> 01:01:21,370
<i>Hey. I told you. That place is lame.</i>

835
01:01:21,453 --> 01:01:23,247
<i>The master of playing by herself.</i>

836
01:01:23,330 --> 01:01:25,541
<i>Nam Da-reum's
legendary solo birthday party.</i>

837
01:01:34,883 --> 01:01:37,386
Are your friends running late?

838
01:01:39,638 --> 01:01:40,806
They'll be here soon.

839
01:01:41,932 --> 01:01:43,058
It's okay.

840
01:02:11,253 --> 01:02:12,296
Mr. Kang.

841
01:02:13,338 --> 01:02:15,340
- Get up.
- Sorry?

842
01:02:30,105 --> 01:02:31,106
Ms. Nam.

843
01:02:32,983 --> 01:02:34,068
Have you been

844
01:02:35,736 --> 01:02:37,071
going on blind dates by any chance?

845
01:02:37,613 --> 01:02:39,448
Blind dates?

846
01:02:39,782 --> 01:02:41,325
Last time, when you asked me
to watch the cats

847
01:02:42,451 --> 01:02:43,535
and even today.

848
01:02:45,245 --> 01:02:46,246
Oh, right.

849
01:02:46,580 --> 01:02:48,290
Yes, it's a blind date.

850
01:02:49,083 --> 01:02:51,043
If you're trying to get over
someone you like

851
01:02:52,711 --> 01:02:53,712
don't bother.

852
01:02:55,714 --> 01:02:56,882
You don't need

853
01:02:58,217 --> 01:02:59,593
to let go of your feelings.

854
01:03:01,678 --> 01:03:03,722
Okay.

855
01:03:04,973 --> 01:03:06,934
Anyway, did he leave without you?

856
01:03:09,144 --> 01:03:10,229
Well...

857
01:03:11,063 --> 01:03:13,649
I was kind of flustered too.

858
01:03:14,399 --> 01:03:16,610
But it happens.

859
01:03:19,363 --> 01:03:21,907
- I'm okay.
- But you're not.

860
01:03:24,910 --> 01:03:26,120
You always say

861
01:03:27,204 --> 01:03:28,247
you're okay.

862
01:03:30,082 --> 01:03:32,084
I guess people won't feel as bad
when you say that.

863
01:03:33,377 --> 01:03:34,878
But you're hurt.

864
01:03:36,463 --> 01:03:37,589
At least, in front of me

865
01:03:39,800 --> 01:03:41,135
you can say it's not okay.

866
01:03:48,142 --> 01:03:49,143
Okay.

867
01:03:50,435 --> 01:03:51,436
To be honest

868
01:03:53,355 --> 01:03:54,648
it wasn't okay.

869
01:03:56,567 --> 01:03:57,734
It's okay.

870
01:04:01,155 --> 01:04:03,031
<i>When I pretend to be okay</i>

871
01:04:07,661 --> 01:04:08,662
<i>I look</i>

872
01:04:10,914 --> 01:04:12,583
<i>less pitiful.</i>

873
01:04:14,793 --> 01:04:17,421
"I'm really fine."

874
01:04:19,840 --> 01:04:22,092
It's really okay.
You should get going.

875
01:04:26,680 --> 01:04:28,557
<i>I've always swallowed it.</i>

876
01:04:30,601 --> 01:04:33,187
But today, it kind of hurts.

877
01:04:33,770 --> 01:04:35,439
Don't meet anyone like that.

878
01:04:38,233 --> 01:04:39,318
Ms. Nam Da-reum.

879
01:04:39,943 --> 01:04:41,486
You deserve better than that.

880
01:04:43,405 --> 01:04:47,075
You don't deserve to date a jerk

881
01:04:48,493 --> 01:04:49,786
who leaves you on a blind date.

882
01:04:58,670 --> 01:05:01,840
<i>That jerk is your friend.</i>

883
01:05:03,133 --> 01:05:04,176
Why are you smiling?

884
01:05:07,971 --> 01:05:09,973
No, it's nothing.

885
01:05:15,312 --> 01:05:17,856
Maybe something more important
than me came up.

886
01:05:19,608 --> 01:05:21,318
Still, for some reason

887
01:05:22,402 --> 01:05:23,695
it's less disappointing today.

888
01:05:24,780 --> 01:05:26,782
Perhaps because I'm walking with you.

889
01:05:29,326 --> 01:05:30,577
I think

890
01:05:31,745 --> 01:05:33,163
I feel better.

891
01:05:33,872 --> 01:05:35,165
The air is nice.

892
01:05:37,960 --> 01:05:39,711
This is a lot better
than the blind date.

893
01:05:47,177 --> 01:05:48,470
I should go home

894
01:05:50,097 --> 01:05:51,306
but I don't want to.

895
01:05:51,974 --> 01:05:53,016
Why not?

896
01:05:56,770 --> 01:05:57,771
Because

897
01:06:00,023 --> 01:06:01,692
I want to stay like this.

898
01:06:02,985 --> 01:06:04,027
Sorry?

899
01:06:07,239 --> 01:06:08,407
Because of Kung.

900
01:06:09,157 --> 01:06:11,576
He doesn't stop running at night
as if he's possessed.

901
01:06:13,120 --> 01:06:14,288
Jjak too.

902
01:06:15,247 --> 01:06:18,250
Apparently, when they're kittens,
they have too much energy to handle.

903
01:06:18,667 --> 01:06:21,461
If Jjak doesn't sleep during the day,
he runs so much at dawn.

904
01:06:21,545 --> 01:06:23,422
So I keep waking up at dawn.

905
01:06:23,797 --> 01:06:26,091
If they live together,
it'll be war every day.

906
01:06:27,092 --> 01:06:28,135
But then

907
01:06:28,593 --> 01:06:31,138
if they stay together,
they'll be less lonely.

908
01:06:36,768 --> 01:06:38,103
This is Jjak from earlier today.

909
01:06:38,437 --> 01:06:41,064
He was enjoying the sunlight,
then he dozed off.

910
01:06:41,606 --> 01:06:42,941
Just like the owner.

911
01:06:43,692 --> 01:06:45,986
So bright and gentle.

912
01:07:01,418 --> 01:07:03,295
It's the first snow this season.

913
01:07:05,505 --> 01:07:06,757
It's pretty.

914
01:07:12,763 --> 01:07:13,805
Yes.

915
01:07:15,849 --> 01:07:17,017
So pretty.

916
01:07:57,641 --> 01:08:01,353
{\an8}MY BIAS, MY BOSS

917
01:08:11,571 --> 01:08:13,824
{\an8}<i>Do you want to meet outside?</i>

918
01:08:14,282 --> 01:08:17,035
{\an8}<i>How can Mr. Kang be fine?</i>

919
01:08:17,119 --> 01:08:18,453
{\an8}He's such a pro.

920
01:08:18,870 --> 01:08:21,123
{\an8}To be honest... Wait!

921
01:08:21,206 --> 01:08:24,042
{\an8}I liked him for a very long time.

922
01:08:24,418 --> 01:08:25,460
{\an8}<i>LA?</i>

923
01:08:25,544 --> 01:08:26,878
{\an8}Why don't you come with me?

924
01:08:27,045 --> 01:08:28,505
{\an8}<i>Whoever he is</i>

925
01:08:28,588 --> 01:08:30,882
{\an8}you don't need to put up
with him that much.

926
01:08:30,966 --> 01:08:32,676
{\an8}<i>Are you protecting your employee</i>

927
01:08:32,759 --> 01:08:33,885
{\an8}or are you keeping me in check?

928
01:08:34,678 --> 01:08:36,847
{\an8}<i>Mr. Kang, the truth is...</i>

929
01:08:37,180 --> 01:08:38,890
{\an8}<i>- Is this...
- Chan, where are you going?</i>

930
01:08:39,099 --> 01:08:40,225
{\an8}<i>Is this true?</i>

931
01:08:44,805 --> 01:08:47,007
{\an8}Synced and corrected by
WEISSACHsubs

